<title>USA: Level One Q4 net income falls.</title>
<headline>Level One Q4 net income falls.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>LEVEL ONE COMMUNICATIONS, INC.</p>
<p>		     CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>For Fiscal years, ended December 29, 1996, and</p>
<p>December, 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (Unaudited)</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>			   (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Dec. 29,    Dec. 30,   Dec. 29  Dec. 30</p>
<p>				  1996	  1995     1996	1995</p>
<p> Revenues		  $29,603     $26,514  $111,987  $78,018</p>
<p> Cost of Sales	    13,612	11,359    48,477   33,300</p>
<p>   Gross margin	   15,991	15,155    63,510   44,718</p>
<p> Research &amp; Development  5,342	 5,616    22,005   17,107</p>
<p> Sales &amp; Marketing	 4,380	 3,487    16,589   11,372</p>
<p>General &amp; Administrative</p>
<p>				 1,615	 1,928     6,741    5,752</p>
<p>Total operating expenses</p>
<p>				11,337	11,031    45,335   34,231</p>
<p> Operating income	  4,654	 4,124    18,175   10,487</p>
<p> Other income, net	   468	   484     2,293    2,064</p>
<p>Income before provision</p>
<p>  for income taxes	 5,122	 4,608    20,468   12,551</p>
<p>One time charge</p>
<p>  for Acquisitions	 2,500	     0     2,500	750</p>
<p>Provision for Income taxes</p>
<p>				 1,690	 (401)     6,755    1,543</p>
<p> Net income		    932	 5,009    11,213   10,258</p>
<p>Earnings per Share:</p>
<p>   EPS			  0.07	  0.37	0.82     0.76</p>
<p>Fully Taxed Excluding</p>
<p>One Time Gain</p>
<p>    and Charge		0.25	  0.23	0.97     0.62</p>
<p>Weighed Average Common</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding    13,957	13,583    13,782   13,465</p>
<p>NOTES: In the second quarter of 1995, the Company incurred a one time charge of $750,000 for the acquisition of San Francisco Telecom.</p>
<p>In the fourth quarter of 1996, the Company incurred a one time charge of $2.5 million related to the acquisition of Silicon Design Experts.</p>
<p>Other income, net includes a one time gain of $675,000 from the sale of Maker Communications stock in the third quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>In the fourth quarter of 1996, the Company incurred a one-time gain of $1.9 million from a tax-adjustment related to the Company's deferred tax asset.</p>
